/-! # Integral specialization of a highest-weight module

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Theorem 22.52 in characteristic zero,
printed p.480, and Section 23h, equations (152)--(153), Theorem 23.72,
printed pp.509--511.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-integral-specialization-highest-weight-dimension)

The root datum is the actual character root datum of the fixed Borel pair.
The highest-vector equation is an equality of coordinate coactions, so it holds
on points over every commutative F-algebra, including nonreduced algebras.
The dimension and all factors of its formula are compared in the rationals.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory CartesianMonoidalCategory
open scoped MonObj TensorProduct

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

open RationalHighestWeight

/-- Every dominant character has a finite-dimensional rational module of Weyl
 dimension with a nonzero Borel eigenvector of that character.

Source: Milne, Theorem 22.52 (characteristic zero only), p.480, and Section 23h,
(152)--(153), Theorem 23.72, pp.509--511.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-integral-specialization-highest-weight-dimension)

Proof plan, following the ten steps of the node:
1. By lem-sfb-simply-connected-character-lattice the character lattice is the full
   weight lattice and roots span its rationalization. Use
   lem-sfb-root-datum-lattice-embedding and lem-sfb-chevalley-admissible-representation
   for rational Chevalley data and an auxiliary faithful full-weight lattice.
2. Apply lem-sfb-rational-highest-weight-modules to eta over Q, with cyclic highest
   vector z. The characteristic-zero formula
   lem-sfb-characteristic-zero-weyl-dimension gives dimension d and the displayed
   product, whose rho-coroot denominators are positive integers.
3. By lem-sfb-kostant-integral-pbw, the actual lattice U_Z z is generated by the
   ordered negative divided-power monomials: positive factors kill z and Cartan
   binomials act integrally. Its rational span is the cyclic module.
4. A finite weight set bounds the total height of every surviving negative
   monomial. Thus finitely many homogeneous monomials generate the lattice.
   Only the empty monomial has weight eta, so its eta summand is exactly Z z.
5. Clear the finitely many coordinate denominators. Apply
   lem-weil-subgroup-finite-free-abelian-group-free to obtain a rank-d free lattice.
   Reduction to F preserves dimension and the direct summand Z z, hence v is nonzero.
6. Root operators are nilpotent by the finite weight set. Apply
   lem-sfb-chevalley-root-exponential-group to the auxiliary faithful module plus
   this module. The generated matrices are block diagonal; projection gives the
   rational action on the reduced lattice, with its actual character weights.
7. Use lem-sfb-root-datum-isogeny-realization with identity lattice map and root
   exponents one to identify the constructed group with G. Pull back its action;
   the weights lie below eta and its top weight space is F v.
8. By lem-sfb-regular-cocharacter-borel-description, B is P(nu) for a regular
   positive cocharacter. Negative Laurent exponents force all matrix entries
   from v to lower weights to vanish over every algebra, including nonreduced
   algebras. Thus B acts on the line through a character restricting to eta.
9. By lem-sfb-bruhat-longest-cell-charts the unipotent radical is affine space;
   its invertible regular functions are constants. This character is therefore
   trivial on the radical. The semidirect decomposition in
   lem-sfb-reductive-borel-pair-structure identifies it with etaB, proving the
   coordinate-coaction identity.
10. The underlying space still has dimension d. Combine steps 2, 5 and 9.
    In rank zero it is F with v = 1 and trivial action; the product is empty.
No simplicity of the reduction or regular-function induction is used. -/
theorem integral_specialization_highest_weight_dimension
    {F : Type u} [Field F] [IsAlgClosed F]
    (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] [CharP F p]
    (G : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (hG : IsSemisimpleGroupScheme G.X)
    (hsc : ∀ (G' : Over (Spec (.of F))) [GrpObj G'],
      IsSemisimpleGroupScheme G' → ∀ (f : G' ⟶ G.X) [IsMonHom f],
      Surjective f.left → IsFinite (GrpObj.ker f).hom →
      (∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra F A]
        (x : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ GrpObj.ker f)
        (g : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ G'),
        (x ≫ GrpObj.kerι f) * g = g * (x ≫ GrpObj.kerι f)) → IsIso f)
    (T B : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iT : T ⟶ G) (iB : B ⟶ G) (j : T ⟶ B)
    (hT : ReductiveTorusCentralizer.IsMaximalTorus iT)
    (hsplit : ∃ r : ℕ, Nonempty (T ≅ MultiplicativeType.splitTorus F r))
    (hB : IsBorelGroupScheme iB.hom.hom) (hj : j ≫ iB = iT)
    [IsCommMonObj T.X] [IsCommMonObj (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)]
    (aG : ModObj T.X G.X) (aB : ModObj T.X B.X)
    (haG : aG.smul = (iT.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 G.X) ≫ CategoryTheory.GrpObj.conj G.X)
    (haB : aB.smul = (j.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 B.X) ≫ CategoryTheory.GrpObj.conj B.X)
    (Φ : Finset (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F))))
    (P : RootDatum Φ
      (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
      (Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)))
    [P.IsReduced] (b : P.Base)
    (hroot : ∀ α : Φ, P.root α = α.val)
    (hpair : ∀ (χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
      (ν : Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)),
      ν.toMul.hom.hom ≫ χ.toMul.hom.hom =
        (𝟙 (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)) ^ (P.toLinearMap χ ν))
    (hweights : ∀ χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)),
      χ ∈ Φ ↔ χ ≠ 0 ∧ @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T G aG χ.toMul ≠ ⊥)
    (hpositive : ∀ α : Φ,
      b.IsPos α ↔ @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T B aB α.val.toMul ≠ ⊥)
    [IsAffine G.X.left] [IsAffine B.X.left]
    (U : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iU : U ⟶ B)
    (hU : IsClosedSubgroupScheme iU.hom.hom ∧ IsNormalSubgroupScheme iU.hom.hom ∧
      Smooth U.X.hom ∧ ConnectedSpace U.X.left ∧ SolvableGroupStructure.IsUnipotent U ∧
      ∀ (N : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iN : N ⟶ B),
        IsClosedSubgroupScheme iN.hom.hom → IsNormalSubgroupScheme iN.hom.hom →
        Smooth N.X.hom → ConnectedSpace N.X.left → SolvableGroupStructure.IsUnipotent N →
        ∃ f : N ⟶ U, f ≫ iU = iN)
    (eta : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
    (hdom : ∀ α ∈ b.support, 0 ≤ P.toLinearMap eta (P.coroot α))
    (etaB : B ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F))
    (hetaB : j ≫ etaB = eta.toMul) (hetaU : iU ≫ etaB = 1)
    (ρ : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
    (hρ : ρ = (1 / 2 : ℚ) •
      ∑ β ∈ (@Finset.filter Φ b.IsPos (Classical.decPred _) Finset.univ),
        TensorProduct.tmul ℤ (1 : ℚ) (P.root β)) :
    (∀ α : Φ, b.IsPos α → ∃ n : ℕ, 0 < n ∧
      (((Int.castAddHom ℚ).toIntLinearMap.comp (P.coroot' α)).liftBaseChange ℚ) ρ = n) ∧
    ∃ (W : Type u) (_ : AddCommGroup W) (_ : Module F W) (_ : FiniteDimensional F W)
      (c : W →ₗ[F] W ⊗[F] coordinateAlgebra G),
      HopfAction.Coassociative F (coordinateAlgebra G) W c ∧
      HopfAction.Counital F (coordinateAlgebra G) W c ∧
      ∃ v : W, v ≠ 0 ∧
        (coordinateMap iB).toLinearMap.lTensor W (c v) = v ⊗ₜ[F] characterElement etaB ∧
        (Module.finrank F W : ℚ) =
          ∏ α ∈ (@Finset.filter Φ b.IsPos (Classical.decPred _) Finset.univ),
            ((((Int.castAddHom ℚ).toIntLinearMap.comp (P.coroot' α)).liftBaseChange ℚ)
              (TensorProduct.tmul ℤ (1 : ℚ) eta + ρ)) /
            ((((Int.castAddHom ℚ).toIntLinearMap.comp (P.coroot' α)).liftBaseChange ℚ) ρ) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
